, 7 of Hearts, 5 of Clubs. There are three clubs on the board, making a flush highly possible for the opponent. My hand is Jack of Hearts and 8 of Hearts. I have no pair and no flush draw (only one heart on board). I have a gutshot straight draw (needing a 9 to make 7-8-9-10-J), but even if I hit it, a flush would beat me. The opponent acted first and checked, showing either weakness or a trap with a made flush. Since I am in position, checking back gives me a free look at the river card to potentially hit my straight or win with a showdown if the opponent is very weak, without risking more chips on a dangerous board.\n\nReason:\nMy hand (High Card Jack) has very little showdown value, and the board texture is wet (3 clubs). Bluffing is risky because the opponent might have a flush or a single club and call. Checking allows me to see the river for free.\n\nAnswer: 0'}
